silm:instances_papers_15_chapters_07_sections_02_concrete_anchor_1#finitelypresentabletestobject silm:hasLongDescription "The FinitelyPresentableTestObject is any specific page-olog schema; e.g. a sub-observation schema like HeadProbe44. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'X', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
